  "worked_solution": "We require a $2\\times 3$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}(-3)x+(-5)y+2z \\\\ 2x+(-3)y+0z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3x-5y+2z \\\\ 2x-3y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
